directive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"max-age","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" directive is sent by a server to indicate that the HTTP response will remain fresh for a specified number of seconds after it is generated."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Essentially, it informs caches how long it will remain fresh. Importantly, the number of seconds indicates the period from which the content was generated,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as opposed to received. This means that any time spent in transit or stored in the caches of intermediaries is deducted from the allowance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"immutable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" directive indicates a guarantee by the server that the HTTP response will not be updated while it is still fresh."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This can be used to avoid unnecessary conditional HTTP requests"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Max-Age cache setting for static centent served by S3 CDN: https:\/\/http.dev\/cache-control."}],"references":{"doc://VernissageServer/documentation/VernissageServer/ArticleVisibilityType":{"title":"ArticleVisibilityType","abstract":[{"text":"Article visibility type.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/vernissageserver\/articlevisibilitytype","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ArticleVisibilityType","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/VernissageServer\/documentation\/VernissageServer\/ArticleVisibilityType","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ArticleVisibilityType","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://VernissageServer/documentation/VernissageServer/MaxAge/Equatable-Implementations":{"title":"Equatable Implementations","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/VernissageServer\/documentation\/VernissageServer\/Ma